msgid "HTTP/3 reference"
msgstr ""

msgid "Overview"
msgstr "Visão geral"

msgid ""
"HTTP/3 is the latest version of the HTTP protocol.\n"
"It replaces TCP with https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc9000[QUIC], a transport protocol built on UDP that provides built-in encryption, reduced connection setup latency, and elimination of head-of-line blocking."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"From an application perspective, HTTP/3 is transparent: request and response handling is identical to HTTP/1.1 and HTTP/2.\n"
"The same handlers, filters, and endpoints work across all three protocols.\n"
"The only differences are at the transport level — QUIC uses UDP instead of TCP, and TLS 1.3 is mandatory."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Quarkus serves HTTP/1.1, HTTP/2, and HTTP/3 on the **same port**.\n"
"Clients discover HTTP/3 availability through the `Alt-Svc` response header on HTTP/1.1 and HTTP/2 responses, then upgrade to QUIC/UDP for subsequent requests."
msgstr ""

msgid "Getting started"
msgstr ""

msgid "Add the `quarkus-http3` extension to your project:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"HTTP/3 requires TLS.\n"
"In **dev and test mode**, a TLS certificate is auto-generated if none is configured (see <<auto-tls>>).\n"
"In **production**, you must configure TLS explicitly — see the xref:tls-registry-reference.adoc[TLS registry reference] for details."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"With TLS in place, HTTP/3 is enabled automatically.\n"
"No additional configuration is needed."
msgstr ""

msgid "Configuration"
msgstr "Configuração"

msgid "Configuration property"
msgstr "Propriedade de configuração"

msgid "Type"
msgstr "Tipo"

msgid "Default"
msgstr "Padrão"

msgid "Description"
msgstr "Descrição"

msgid "`quarkus.http3.enabled`"
msgstr ""

msgid "boolean"
msgstr "booleano"

msgid "`true`"
msgstr "`true`"

msgid ""
"Whether HTTP/3 (QUIC) support is enabled.\n"
"When enabled and the native QUIC library is on the classpath, HTTP/3 is added to the set of supported HTTP versions on the HTTPS server."
msgstr ""

msgid "`quarkus.http3.alt-svc`"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Whether to add the `Alt-Svc` response header to HTTP/1.1 and HTTP/2 responses on the HTTPS server, advertising HTTP/3 availability.\n"
"The header value follows the format `h3=\":PORT\"; ma=MAX_AGE`."
msgstr ""

msgid "`quarkus.http3.alt-svc-max-age`"
msgstr ""

msgid "Duration"
msgstr ""

msgid "`24H`"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The `max-age` value included in the `Alt-Svc` header.\n"
"Tells clients how long to cache the HTTP/3 advertisement before re-checking via HTTP/1.1 or HTTP/2.\n"
"Only effective when `quarkus.http3.alt-svc` is `true`."
msgstr ""

msgid "Auto-TLS in dev and test mode"
msgstr ""

msgid "When the HTTP/3 extension is on the classpath and no TLS configuration is detected, Quarkus auto-generates a certificate in dev and test mode:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"If the **Quarkus Dev CA** exists at `~/.quarkus/quarkus-dev-root-ca.pem`, the certificate is signed by it.\n"
"Browsers and clients that trust the Dev CA will accept the certificate without warnings."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Otherwise, a **self-signed certificate** is generated.\n"
"Browsers will show a certificate warning, which is acceptable for development."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"When auto-TLS is active, plain HTTP requests are **redirected to HTTPS** by default.\n"
"To allow plain HTTP alongside HTTPS, set:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"In **production mode**, no auto-generation occurs.\n"
"If TLS is not configured, the server fails at startup with a clear error message."
msgstr ""

